Take a seat.

1918
02:18:57,496 --> 02:18:59,455
Just relax.

1919
02:19:00,499 --> 02:19:03,125
This is to remove your collar.

1920
02:19:04,545 --> 02:19:06,003
[BOLT CLICKS]

1921
02:19:51,341 --> 02:19:52,592
Nay.

1922
02:20:12,070 --> 02:20:13,529
No.

1923
02:20:13,697 --> 02:20:15,406
[ZACHRY SOBBING]

1924
02:20:15,574 --> 02:20:16,574
Nay.

1925
02:20:19,369 --> 02:20:20,995
Rose.

1926
02:20:21,747 --> 02:20:22,747
Rose.

1927
02:20:48,190 --> 02:20:50,191
[PERSON SNORING]

1928
02:21:21,431 --> 02:21:24,934
<i>ABBESS:
Enemy's sleeping, don't slit that throat.</i>

1929
02:21:37,155 --> 02:21:39,156
[GRUNTING THEN SCREAMING]

1930
02:22:10,147 --> 02:22:14,525
Their genomics industry demands
a huge quantity of biomatter for wombtanks.

1931
02:22:15,152 --> 02:22:18,821
But more importantly,
to sustain their engineered labor force.

1932
02:22:19,448 --> 02:22:23,200
Recycled Fabricants are
a cheap source of protein.

1933
02:22:24,369 --> 02:22:25,661
Soap.

1934
02:22:28,582 --> 02:22:31,876
They feed us to ourselves.

1935
02:22:42,846 --> 02:22:44,346
That ship...

1936
02:22:47,309 --> 02:22:49,894
That ship must be destroyed.

1937
02:22:52,022 --> 02:22:53,022
Yes.

1938
02:22:53,398 --> 02:22:57,651
The systems that built them
must be torn down.

1939
02:22:59,112 --> 02:23:00,362
Yes.

1940
02:23:01,698 --> 02:23:08,370
No matter if we are born in a tank
or a womb, we are all Pureblood.

1941
02:23:10,499 --> 02:23:11,499
Yes.

1942
02:23:13,877 --> 02:23:16,045
We must all fight...

1943
02:23:17,005 --> 02:23:19,381
...and, if necessary, die...

1944
02:23:20,050 --> 02:23:24,011
...to teach people the truth.

1945
02:23:32,604 --> 02:23:35,189
This is what we have been waiting for.

1946
02:23:41,863 --> 02:23:43,197
<i>FROBISHER:
It's done.</i>

1947
02:23:54,501 --> 02:23:55,543
[GASPS]

1948
02:23:55,710 --> 02:23:58,796
Oh. Oh. Here, here, Catkin.

1949
02:23:59,297 --> 02:24:03,300
Oh. Oh, Catkin. Oh.

1950
02:24:05,470 --> 02:24:07,471
[HORSE NEIGHS]

1951
02:24:07,639 --> 02:24:09,473
[HOOFBEATS APPROACHING]

1952
02:24:10,183 --> 02:24:12,101
- Shh.
- No.

1953
02:24:22,654 --> 02:24:23,696
[WHISTLES]

1954
02:24:52,058 --> 02:24:53,100
[GRUNTS]

1955
02:24:56,104 --> 02:24:57,271
[SCREAMS]

1956
02:25:04,613 --> 02:25:08,657
<i>ARCHIVIST: You were then taken
to a Union-controlled satellite link.</i>

1957
02:25:09,367 --> 02:25:11,702
<i>SONMl-451:
I broadcast my Revelation...</i>

1958
02:25:11,870 --> 02:25:15,289
...to the Twelve States
and Four Off-World Colonies.

1959
02:25:16,291 --> 02:25:20,294
Eighteen minutes later,
the Enforcers attacked.

1960
02:25:21,213 --> 02:25:22,338
[STATIC CRACKLING]

1961
02:25:22,505 --> 02:25:25,257
<i>SONMl-451 [OVER RADIO]:
To be is to be perceived.</i>

1962
02:25:25,884 --> 02:25:30,804
And so to know thyself is only possible
through the eyes of the other.

1963
02:25:34,226 --> 02:25:38,562
The nature of our immortal lives
is in the consequences of our words...

1964
02:25:39,397 --> 02:25:43,567
...and deeds that go on
apportioning themselves...

1965
02:25:43,777 --> 02:25:45,903
...throughout all time.

1966
02:25:56,748 --> 02:25:58,123
[KONAS YELLING]

1967
02:26:13,431 --> 02:26:15,891
Zachry.

1968
02:26:18,228 --> 02:26:19,270
[LAUGHING]

1969
02:26:19,437 --> 02:26:20,437
CATKIN:
Unc'a Zach!

1970
02:26:28,530 --> 02:26:30,572
ZACHRY:
Hide, hide!

1971
02:26:50,635 --> 02:26:51,802
<i>ADAM:
Zachry!</i>

1972
02:26:52,220 --> 02:26:54,638
No! No! No!

1973
02:26:57,475 --> 02:27:00,394
You kill chief. Now you meat.

1974
02:27:09,237 --> 02:27:10,571
[BOTH GROAN]

1975
02:27:13,992 --> 02:27:15,409
[GROANS]

1976
02:27:22,334 --> 02:27:24,001
[CHOKING]

1977
02:27:30,800 --> 02:27:32,509
[YELLING]

1978
02:27:33,219 --> 02:27:34,553
[MERONYM YELLS]

1979
02:27:41,686 --> 02:27:43,020
[ZACHRY GRUNTS]

1980
02:27:43,396 --> 02:27:45,105
[GROANS]

1981
02:27:47,317 --> 02:27:49,401
[BOTH YELLING]

1982
02:27:53,698 --> 02:27:55,699
[PANTING]

1983
02:27:56,701 --> 02:27:58,410
[PANTING]

1984
02:28:02,999 --> 02:28:04,124
ZACHRY:
Catkin.

1985
02:28:04,542 --> 02:28:06,335
- Safe now.
CATKIN: Unc'a Zach!

1986
02:28:06,544 --> 02:28:08,670
Safe, safe now.

1987
02:28:13,176 --> 02:28:14,635
Thank Sonmi.

1988
02:28:15,136 --> 02:28:17,554
No, thank you.

1989
02:28:26,940 --> 02:28:29,817
Come on, Mr. Ewing, one more.

1990
02:28:31,236 --> 02:28:32,528
One more.

1991
02:28:32,695 --> 02:28:34,822
Salt clean out your stomach.

1992
02:28:37,867 --> 02:28:39,493
Good, good.

1993
02:28:39,661 --> 02:28:42,496
Come on, Mr. Ewing, come on. Come on.

1994
02:28:46,376 --> 02:28:49,753
See where we are?
See where we are? Stay here.

1995
02:28:52,674 --> 02:28:53,841
Home.

1996
02:28:54,551 --> 02:28:55,843
Home.

1997
02:29:00,765 --> 02:29:02,099
Megan Sixsmith?

1998
02:29:13,236 --> 02:29:14,278
Make them pay.

1999
02:29:19,200 --> 02:29:20,993
You can count on it.

2000
02:29:30,545 --> 02:29:31,545
Thank you.

2001
02:29:35,884 --> 02:29:41,805
My uncle was a scientist,
but he believed that love was real...

2002
02:29:42,807 --> 02:29:46,310
...a kind of natural phenomenon.

2003
02:29:49,147 --> 02:29:50,647
He believed that...

2004
02:29:50,815 --> 02:29:53,442
<i>...love could outlive death.</i>

2005
02:29:57,655 --> 02:30:01,617
<i>FROBISHER: Finished in a frenzy that
reminded me of our last night in Cambridge.</i>

2006
02:30:03,036 --> 02:30:07,080
<i>Watched my final sunrise,
enjoyed a last cigarette.</i>

2007
02:30:07,665 --> 02:30:09,833
<i>Didn't think the view
could be any more perfect...</i>

2008
02:30:10,293 --> 02:30:12,085
<i>...until I saw that beat-up trilby.</i>

2009
02:30:14,464 --> 02:30:18,258
<i>Honestly, Sixsmith, as ridiculous
as that thing makes you look...</i>

2010
02:30:18,843 --> 02:30:21,512
<i>...I don't believe I've ever seen
anything more beautiful.</i>

2011
02:30:28,353 --> 02:30:30,687
<i>Watched you for as long as I dared.</i>

2012
02:30:33,274 --> 02:30:37,277
<i>I don't believe it was a fluke
that I saw you first.</i>

2013
02:30:40,657 --> 02:30:42,616
- Okay.
MERONYM: Thank you.

2014
02:30:44,619 --> 02:30:46,119
DUOPHYSITE:
Corporal, update the log book...

2015
02:30:46,287 --> 02:30:49,623
- ... and make sure there is a cabin...
- Captain say-soed take you with us.

2016
02:30:49,958 --> 02:30:51,500
I wanna go with Meronym.

2017
02:30:51,668 --> 02:30:53,293
Go where?

2018
02:30:54,337 --> 02:30:56,797
Prescients n'same boat as us.

2019
02:30:56,965 --> 02:30:59,049
Got no home neitherwise.

2020
02:31:00,718 --> 02:31:03,804
Nay... not yet.

2021
02:31:05,598 --> 02:31:10,227
You think someone going to hear
your prayer, come down from the sky?

2022
02:31:11,479 --> 02:31:14,398
P'haps. P'haps one day.

2023
02:31:14,566 --> 02:31:17,234
Heh. One day ain't but a flea o' hope.

2024
02:31:18,111 --> 02:31:20,654
Yay, and fleas ain't so easy to rid.

2025
02:31:22,407 --> 02:31:24,408
ZACHRY:
Hm.

2026
02:31:34,627 --> 02:31:38,005
<i>FROBISHER: I believe there is
another world waiting for us, Sixsmith.</i>

2027
02:31:38,256 --> 02:31:39,673
<i>A better world...</i>

2028
02:31:40,592 --> 02:31:42,551
<i>...and I'll be waiting for you there.</i>

2029
02:31:45,263 --> 02:31:46,847
May I help you, sir?

2030
02:31:47,015 --> 02:31:50,142
Yes, thank you, I'm looking for
a friend who came to Edin...

2031
02:31:50,435 --> 02:31:51,435
...burgh.

2032
02:31:56,733 --> 02:31:59,359
<i>FROBISHER:
I believe we do not stay dead long.</i>

2033
02:32:01,154 --> 02:32:04,865
<i>Find me beneath the Corsican stars
where we first kissed.</i>

2034
02:32:06,284 --> 02:32:10,037
<i>Yours eternally, R.F.</i>

2035
02:32:32,810 --> 02:32:34,811
[GUNSHOT]

2036
02:32:52,538 --> 02:32:53,664
No!

2037
02:33:03,966 --> 02:33:05,008
God!

2038
02:33:07,011 --> 02:33:08,011
No!

2039
02:33:11,516 --> 02:33:13,517
[SOBBING]

2040
02:33:19,273 --> 02:33:22,609
The report said Commander Chang
was killed in the assault.

2041
02:33:24,028 --> 02:33:25,696
That is correct.

2042
02:33:27,365 --> 02:33:29,408
Would you say that you loved him?

2043
02:33:31,119 --> 02:33:32,536
Yes, I do.

2044
02:33:33,913 --> 02:33:36,748
Do you mean you are
still in love with him?

2045
02:33:37,792 --> 02:33:40,377
I mean that I will always be.

2046
02:33:43,715 --> 02:33:46,550
Our lives are not our own.

2047
02:33:48,052 --> 02:33:50,554
From womb to tomb...

2048
02:33:51,139 --> 02:33:53,432
...we are bound to others...

2049
02:33:55,893 --> 02:33:57,519
...past and present...

2050
02:34:06,529 --> 02:34:10,407
...and by each crime
and every kindness...

2051
02:34:11,743 --> 02:34:14,411
...we birth our future.

2052
02:34:16,831 --> 02:34:18,832
[EXPLOSION]

2053
02:34:25,339 --> 02:34:27,340
[SOBBING]

2054
02:34:38,686 --> 02:34:42,314
In your Revelation, you spoke of
the consequences of an individual's life...

2055
02:34:42,482 --> 02:34:45,108
...rippling throughout eternity.

2056
02:34:48,780 --> 02:34:51,615
Does this mean that you believe
in an afterlife?

2057
02:34:52,784 --> 02:34:55,118
In a heaven or a hell?

2058
02:34:57,789 --> 02:35:02,209
I believe death is only a door.

2059
02:35:03,795 --> 02:35:07,214
When it closes, another opens.

2060
02:35:09,634 --> 02:35:11,968
If I cared to imagine a heaven...

2061
02:35:12,720 --> 02:35:15,096
...I would imagine a door opening...

2062
02:35:17,141 --> 02:35:18,725
<i>...and behind it...</i>

2063
02:35:20,186 --> 02:35:22,229
<i>...I would find him there...</i>

2064
02:35:22,647 --> 02:35:24,314
...waiting for me.

2065
02:35:27,902 --> 02:35:29,569
- Oh!
- Oh, Tilda!

2066
02:35:33,908 --> 02:35:36,159
I'm home. I'm home.

2067
02:35:36,869 --> 02:35:38,328
I'm home.

2068
02:35:41,249 --> 02:35:43,667
Oh, God, I missed you so much!

2069
02:35:50,716 --> 02:35:52,008
MAN:
Thank you, sir.

2070
02:35:54,053 --> 02:35:56,680
If I may ask one last question:

2071
02:35:57,431 --> 02:36:00,267
You had to know this Union scheme
was doomed to fail.

2072
02:36:01,018 --> 02:36:02,060
Yes.

2073
02:36:02,270 --> 02:36:04,396
Then why did you agree to it?

2074
02:36:05,106 --> 02:36:08,483
This is what General Apis asked of me.

2075
02:36:09,026 --> 02:36:11,069
What, to be executed?

2076
02:36:11,612 --> 02:36:16,241
If I had remained invisible,
the truth would stay hidden.

2077
02:36:16,534 --> 02:36:18,535
I couldn't allow that.

2078
02:36:20,955 --> 02:36:24,583
And what if no one believes this truth?

2079
02:36:27,336 --> 02:36:29,462
Someone already does.

2080
02:36:33,593 --> 02:36:35,093
[HANDCUFFS CRACKLE THEN CLANG]

2081
02:36:42,894 --> 02:36:44,561
[DOOR CLOSES]

2082
02:36:44,896 --> 02:36:46,897
[ALL CHUCKLING]

2083
02:36:49,066 --> 02:36:50,692
Adam? Good God!

2084
02:36:50,860 --> 02:36:54,404
I have just been recounting
your astonishing adventure.

2085
02:36:54,739 --> 02:36:55,906
Please join us.

2086
02:36:56,073 --> 02:36:57,073
Get him a chair.

2087
02:36:57,241 --> 02:36:59,826
No, no, thank you. I cannot stay.

2088
02:37:00,077 --> 02:37:01,661
Well, what are you doing here?

2089
02:37:01,829 --> 02:37:04,539
I thought the doctor said
at least three weeks in bed.

2090
02:37:04,749 --> 02:37:07,292
He did, but this couldn't wait.

2091
02:37:08,628 --> 02:37:11,046
I need to speak with you, sir. Privately.

2092
02:37:11,255 --> 02:37:12,589
Of course.

2093
02:37:13,591 --> 02:37:14,799
Excuse me.

2094
02:37:21,098 --> 02:37:24,100
Is that the contract from
Reverend Horrox?

2095
02:37:25,519 --> 02:37:26,561
It is indeed.

2096
02:37:26,771 --> 02:37:28,939
Well, you know, I could have sent a boy.

2097
02:37:34,570 --> 02:37:36,613
Are you insane?!

2098
02:37:36,781 --> 02:37:40,158
I owe my life to a self-freed slave.

2099
02:37:41,994 --> 02:37:47,082
And I cannot in good conscience participate
in this kind of business any longer.

2100
02:37:49,085 --> 02:37:51,211
JAVIER:
This would make such a good book.

2101
02:37:51,629 --> 02:37:53,004
I'll drink to that.

2102
02:37:55,132 --> 02:37:57,133
[BOTH IMITATE GLASSES CLINKING]

2103
02:38:03,140 --> 02:38:08,937
<i>CAVENDISH: Outside, fat snowflakes
are falling on slate roofs and granite walls.</i>

2104
02:38:09,105 --> 02:38:10,105
[TYPEWRITER CLACKING]

2105
02:38:10,272 --> 02:38:14,567
<i>Like Solzhenitsyn laboring in Vermont,
I shall beaver away in exile.</i>

2106
02:38:15,653 --> 02:38:19,364
<i>Unlike Solzhenitsyn, I shan't be alone.</i>

2107
02:38:31,711 --> 02:38:36,423
Goddamn you, sir.
If you were not my daughter's husband-

2108
02:38:36,590 --> 02:38:38,341
TILDA:
Hello, Father.

2109
02:38:38,718 --> 02:38:39,884
MOORE:
Tilda?

2110
02:38:42,930 --> 02:38:44,264
What is going on?

2111
02:38:44,974 --> 02:38:46,641
I've come to say goodbye.

2112
02:38:46,851 --> 02:38:48,768
Goodbye? Where are you going?

2113
02:38:49,520 --> 02:38:53,064
We're moving back East
to work with the Abolitionists.

2114
02:38:53,566 --> 02:38:54,691
What?

2115
02:38:55,860 --> 02:38:59,612
That poison has rotted your brain.

2116
02:39:00,072 --> 02:39:02,699
Well, if it has, I highly recommend it.

2117
02:39:02,908 --> 02:39:04,701
I've not felt this good in years.

2118
02:39:05,161 --> 02:39:08,496
Tilda, I forbid you from going anywhere
with this madman.

2119
02:39:09,665 --> 02:39:12,459
I've been afraid of you
my whole life, Father.

2120
02:39:15,546 --> 02:39:17,672
I'm going with my husband.

2121
02:39:22,887 --> 02:39:23,887
Adam!

2122
02:39:27,975 --> 02:39:29,517
Listen to me.

2123
02:39:30,186 --> 02:39:33,438
For the sake of my grandson,
if not your own.

2124
02:39:33,939 --> 02:39:36,816
There is a natural order to this world...

2125
02:39:36,984 --> 02:39:40,779
...and those who try to upend it
do not fare well.

2126
02:39:42,406 --> 02:39:45,116
<i>This movement will never survive.</i>

2127
02:39:45,910 --> 02:39:49,996
<i>If you join them, you and your
entire family will be shunned.</i>

2128
02:39:50,498 --> 02:39:54,667
<i>At best, you'll exist as pariah
to be spat on and beaten.</i>

2129
02:39:55,753 --> 02:39:59,047
<i>At worst, lynched or crucified.</i>

2130
02:40:16,982 --> 02:40:18,650
And for what?

2131
02:40:20,444 --> 02:40:21,820
For what?

2132
02:40:22,113 --> 02:40:23,780
No matter what you do...

2133
02:40:23,948 --> 02:40:28,576
...it will never amount to anything more
than a single drop in a limitless ocean.

2134
02:40:29,954 --> 02:40:33,832
But what is an ocean
but a multitude of drops?

2135
02:40:46,679 --> 02:40:48,513
Well, firey dyin'.

2136
02:40:49,974 --> 02:40:52,809
Mm. Just as well. My yarning is done.

2137
02:40:52,977 --> 02:40:54,811
CHILDREN:
No! Please!

2138
02:40:54,979 --> 02:40:56,312
BOY:
Tell us one more!

2139
02:40:56,480 --> 02:40:57,856
[CHILDREN SPEAKING INDISTINCTLY]

2140
02:40:58,023 --> 02:41:00,650
MERONYM: Come on in here,
you little buggers! Come on, it's gettin' cold!

2141
02:41:00,818 --> 02:41:04,487
Uh, now, you heard your Grammy.
Go on. Get on with ya. Come on.

2142
02:41:04,655 --> 02:41:06,030
Eh? Eh?

2143
02:41:06,198 --> 02:41:08,199
[CHILDREN GIGGLING]

2144
02:41:15,916 --> 02:41:18,626
You like it out here, don'tcha, Grampy?

2145
02:41:19,420 --> 02:41:23,173
Supposin' it minders me
of my Valley, huh?

2146
02:41:23,757 --> 02:41:25,258
Which is Earth?

2147
02:41:26,594 --> 02:41:28,344
Uh... There.

2148
02:41:28,637 --> 02:41:31,514
That one there. That blue shimmerer.

2149
02:41:32,308 --> 02:41:33,725
Yeah.

2150
02:41:36,896 --> 02:41:39,022
Now, help your Grampy up.

2151
02:41:40,316 --> 02:41:41,649
Oh, yeah.

2152
02:41:43,194 --> 02:41:44,944
Are you gonna tell us
'bout the woahsome ship...

2153
02:41:45,112 --> 02:41:48,239
...and the big sleep
and all the nex'nexs?

2154
02:41:48,407 --> 02:41:52,202
ZACHRY: No, your grammy tells
the nex'nexs way better than me.

2155
02:41:53,787 --> 02:41:55,413
Do you still love Grammy?

2156
02:41:58,542 --> 02:42:02,921
Your grammy is the best thing
that ever happened to me.

2157
02:42:08,010 --> 02:42:11,262
ZACHRY: Mm.
MERONYM: Come on here, Grampy.

2158
02:42:11,597 --> 02:42:13,723
Lemme warm them old bones.

2159
02:42:13,891 --> 02:42:16,226
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

2160
02:51:53,220 --> 02:51:55,221
[English - US - SDH]

